<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Veera Ballala III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1292–1343</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Vira Ballala III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Veera Ballala III was the last major king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala Empire</a>, ruling from 1292 to 1343. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-kafur">Malik Kafur</a>, general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a>, sacked his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwarasamudra">Dwarasamudra</a> in 1311 and forced him to pay tribute. He later rebuilt Hoysala power and resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai-sultanate">Madurai Sultanate</a>, but was captured and killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> sultan in 1343. Former Hoysala commanders went on to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>.</p></div>
